---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Student Experience & Operational Analytics \u2014 Shailly | Work Sample" description="Kraftshala Program Management work sample: a four-scenario student support framework and operational analytics across cancellations, session delays, batch performance, and expert reliability." path="/work/samples/kraftshala-assignment/" ogType="article" ogTitle="Student Experience & Operational Analytics \u2014 Shailly">
  <article>
    <header class="case-hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <nav class="breadcrumb mono" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
          <a href="/work/">Selected Work</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
          <span>Work sample 01</span>
        </nav>

        <div class="page-head-grid">
          <div>
            <p class="mono case-cat">Work sample 01 &middot; Independent</p>
            <h1>Student Experience &amp; Operational Analytics</h1>
            <p class="sample-sub">A two-part program management hiring assignment exploring student support, operational problem-solving, and data-driven decision-making.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="head-fact reveal">
            <span class="mono">Context</span>
            <dl>
              <dt class="mono">Label</dt>
              <dd>Independent work sample submitted as part of the Kraftshala Program Management selection process, 2026.</dd>
              <dt class="mono">Parts</dt>
              <dd>Student experience &amp; problem-solving &middot; Operational analytics</dd>
            </dl>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="meta-strip reveal">
        <div class="meta-cell"><span class="k">Type</span><span class="v">Independent work sample</span></div>
        <div class="meta-cell"><span class="k">Part 1</span><span class="v">Student experience &amp; problem-solving</span></div>
        <div class="meta-cell"><span class="k">Part 2</span><span class="v">Operational analytics</span></div>
        <div class="meta-cell"><span class="k">Tools</span><span class="v">Excel &middot; structured decision framework</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="cs-section">
      <div class="wrap cs-grid">
        <div class="cs-label"><span class="n">01</span><h2>Part 1 &mdash; Student experience</h2></div>
        <div class="cs-body">
          <p class="lead">Analysing a hypothetical conversation between a Program Manager and a student struggling to meet program requirements because of family responsibilities.</p>
          <p>My assessment considered both the student&rsquo;s circumstances and the program&rsquo;s operational constraints. Rather than treating the situation solely as a compliance issue, I identified the need to balance student support with clear expectations.</p>

          <div class="framework">
            <div class="fw-step"><span class="mono">01</span><strong>Evaluate the conversation</strong><p>Rapport, empathy, information gathering, solution exploration.</p></div>
            <div class="fw-step"><span class="mono">02</span><strong>Find the gaps</strong><p>Alternative explanations and missing context.</p></div>
            <div class="fw-step"><span class="mono">03</span><strong>Structure the situation</strong><p>A repeatable approach to understanding it.</p></div>
            <div class="fw-step"><span class="mono">04</span><strong>Establish constraints</strong><p>What the program can and cannot flex.</p></div>
            <div class="fw-step"><span class="mono">05</span><strong>Build four scenarios</strong><p>Different intervention plans and owners.</p></div>
            <div class="fw-step"><span class="mono">06</span><strong>Define closure</strong><p>Actions, responsibilities, follow-ups, closure criteria.</p></div>
          </div>

          <div class="artefacts">
            <h3 class="mono">Supporting artefacts</h3>
            <div class="artefact-grid">
              <div class="artefact"><span class="mono">01</span>Post-call communication template</div>
              <div class="artefact"><span class="mono">02</span>Internal call note</div>
              <div class="artefact"><span class="mono">03</span>Student action plan</div>
              <div class="artefact"><span class="mono">04</span>Four-scenario decision framework</div>
              <div class="artefact"><span class="mono">05</span>Scenario-based process flowchart</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p>The emphasis was on separating what was known from what was assumed, and turning a difficult conversation into a documented plan with owners and next steps.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cs-section">
      <div class="wrap cs-grid">
        <div class="cs-label"><span class="n">02</span><h2>Part 2 &mdash; Operational analytics</h2></div>
        <div class="cs-body">
          <p class="lead">I analysed operational data relating to session joining times, cancellations, batch-level performance, and expert reliability.</p>
          <p>The objective was to translate raw operational data into meaningful insights and recommendations.</p>

          <div class="data-panel" role="figure" aria-label="Illustrative operational dashboard with reconstructed figures">
            <div class="data-bar mono">
              <span>Operations review / week-on-week</span>
              <span class="tagline">Illustrative &mdash; reconstructed figures</span>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi-row">
              <div class="kpi"><span class="k mono">On-time sessions</span><b>44%</b></div>
              <div class="kpi"><span class="k mono">&ldquo;Other&rdquo; cancellations</span><b>38%</b></div>
              <div class="kpi"><span class="k mono">Avg. positive delay</span><b>24.7<span class="unit">min</span></b></div>
              <div class="kpi"><span class="k mono">Batch 40 on-time</span><b>24.4%</b></div>
            </div>
            <div class="chart" aria-hidden="true">
              <div class="chart-axis mono"><span>Week 1</span><span>Week 2</span></div>
              <div class="chart-bars">
                <div class="cb"><span style="--v:26%"></span><em class="mono">2.8</em><small class="mono">Batch 35 delay</small></div>
                <div class="cb"><span style="--v:92%"></span><em class="mono">24.7</em><small class="mono">Batch 35 delay</small></div>
                <div class="cb"><span style="--v:45%"></span><em class="mono">7.5%</em><small class="mono">Batch 40 cancel</small></div>
                <div class="cb"><span style="--v:71%"></span><em class="mono">11.8%</em><small class="mono">Batch 40 cancel</small></div>
                <div class="cb"><span style="--v:44%"></span><em class="mono">45.1%</em><small class="mono">Batch 40 on time</small></div>
                <div class="cb"><span style="--v:24%"></span><em class="mono">24.4%</em><small class="mono">Batch 40 on time</small></div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="tracker-note"><span class="mark" aria-hidden="true">&#9656;</span> <a href="https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/13-dX96VzSMuPkVERijH9RIs9kqffNOZjAcoEktfxztY/edit" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the original workbook in Google Sheets <span aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</span></a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cs-section">
      <div class="wrap cs-grid">
        <div class="cs-label"><span class="n">03</span><h2>Findings &amp; recommendations</h2></div>
        <div class="cs-body">
          <div class="findings">
            <div class="finding">
              <span class="f-num mono">Insight 01</span>
              <div class="f-main">
                <h3>Cancellation categorisation</h3>
                <p>Approximately 38% of cancellations were categorised as &ldquo;Other&rdquo;.</p>
              </div>
              <p class="f-rec"><span class="mono">Recommendation</span>Improve cancellation reason categorisation and make it mandatory.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="finding">
              <span class="f-num mono">Insight 02</span>
              <div class="f-main">
                <h3>Batch 35 delay</h3>
                <p>Average positive delay increased from approximately 2.8 minutes to 24.7 minutes between the two weeks.</p>
              </div>
              <p class="f-rec"><span class="mono">Recommendation</span>Investigate individual sessions before making broader operational changes.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="finding">
              <span class="f-num mono">Insight 03</span>
              <div class="f-main">
                <h3>Batch 40 performance</h3>
                <p>Cancellation rate increased from approximately 7.5% to 11.8%, while on-time joining decreased from approximately 45.1% to 24.4%.</p>
              </div>
              <p class="f-rec"><span class="mono">Recommendation</span>Investigate scheduling conflicts, expert availability, and short-notice cancellations.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="finding">
              <span class="f-num mono">Insight 04</span>
              <div class="f-main">
                <h3>Session punctuality</h3>
                <p>Only around 44% of sessions were on time or early.</p>
              </div>
              <p class="f-rec"><span class="mono">Recommendation</span>Investigate widespread minor delays, session transitions, scheduling buffers, and expert readiness.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="finding">
              <span class="f-num mono">Insight 05</span>
              <div class="f-main">
                <h3>Expert reliability</h3>
                <p>Expert-level performance varied across punctuality, delays, and cancellations.</p>
              </div>
              <p class="f-rec"><span class="mono">Recommendation</span>Identify recurring patterns while accounting for the number of sessions handled by each expert.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="callout" style="margin-top:1.8rem">
            <span class="mono callout-label">Analytical approach</span>
            <p>An important part of the analysis was distinguishing between an observed metric and a confirmed cause. Where performance changed sharply, I recommended investigating the underlying sessions and operational factors before implementing broader interventions.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cs-section">
      <div class="wrap cs-grid">
        <div class="cs-label"><span class="n">04</span><h2>The workbook</h2></div>
        <div class="cs-body">
          <p class="lead">A five-view analytical workbook.</p>
          <div class="artefacts">
            <div class="artefact-grid">
              <div class="artefact"><span class="mono">01</span>Week-on-week dashboard</div>
              <div class="artefact"><span class="mono">02</span>Expert performance scorecard</div>
              <div class="artefact"><span class="mono">03</span>Cleaned joining data</div>
              <div class="artefact"><span class="mono">04</span>Cleaned cancellation data</div>
              <div class="artefact"><span class="mono">05</span>Chart data</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="evidence-note">
            <span class="mono">Privacy</span>
            <p>The original workbook is not published. It contains identifiable session and expert data; the visuals shown here are reconstructions.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="next-project" aria-label="Next work sample">
        <div>
          <span class="mono np-label">Next work sample / 02</span>
          <a href="/work/samples/ui-fellowship-presentation/"><span class="np-title">U&amp;I Fellowship &mdash; Program Design &amp; Recruitment Operations &rarr;</span></a>
        </div>
        <a class="link-arrow" href="/work/">All selected work <span aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</span></a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
